game (
	name "Geom Cube (USA)"
	serial "SLUS-00024"
	description "In the tradition of Tetris and Welltris comes Geom Cube, a puzzle game in which players maneuver 3D blocks as they fall into a pit. The twist is that players are looking down from a view directly above the pit. Each falling block can be rotated on its axis, allowing for a variety of ways to fit the puzzle pieces together. The objective is to create a solid plane of blocks in order to prevent others from piling up to the top of the playfield. Creating a plane of blocks without gaps (called a 'face') causes the blocks on that plane to disappear. There are 24 different block patterns in all, each composed of one to five cubes."
	developer "Technos"
	publisher "Technos"
	releaseyear "1995"
	releasemonth "12"
	releaseday "10"
