game (
	name "Vadims (Japan)"
	serial "SLPS-00352"
	description "Vadims is a classic puzzle game in the style of the Tetris series designed by Vadim Gerasimov an engineer at Google. In 1994-2003 Vadim worked and studied at the MIT Media Lab. At age 16 he was one of the original co-developers of the famous video game Tetris: he ported Alexey Pajitnov's original game to the PC architecture and the two later added features to the game. Vadim earned a BS/MS in applied mathematics from Moscow State University in 1992 and a Ph.D. from MIT in 2003."
