		name "NFL Blitz 2000 (Europe).cue"
	)
)

game (
	name "NFL Gameday (Europe)"
	serial "SCES-00219"
	description "Calling all armchair football fanatics -- NFL GameDay brings tackles, fumbles, field goals and touchdowns to your living room with a full National Football League license. Featuring rendered 3D graphics, the developers have crammed over 1,500 actual football players along with 30 NFL teams and their respective stadiums onto a single PlayStation disc. Because of the licensing, each team's logo and end-zone visuals have been represented; jersey colors (both home and away) are authentic to the sport."
	developer "Sony"
	publisher "Sony"
	releaseyear "1996"
	releasemonth "5"
	releaseday "10"
	users "2"
	genre "Football"
	rom (
		serial "SCES-00219"
		name "NFL Gameday (Europe).cue"
	)
)

game (
	name "NFL Quarterback Club '97 (Europe)"
	serial "SLES-00449"
	description "NFL Quarterback Club '97 from Acclaim makes a splash on the PlayStation console. Everything you'd expect from a football title can be found in NFL Quarterback Club '97. You have all the standard gameplay options: exhibition, season, quick play. Then you have all the standard options that are looked for in a football game. Players act like their real-life counterpart, complete with juking moves, stiff arms, laterals, diving over the top, and much, much more. Take your favorite team all the way through the season and see if you have what it takes to make it to the Super Bowl, or start from the playoffs altogether."
	developer "Iguana Entertainment"
	publisher "Acclaim"
	releaseyear "1996"
	releasemonth "11"
	releaseday "30"
	users "8"
	genre "Football"
	rom (
		serial "SLES-00449"
		name "NFL Quarterback Club '97 (Europe).cue"
	)
)

game (
	name "NFL Xtreme (Europe)"
	serial "SCES-01490"
	description "Like NFL Blitz, NFL Xtreme is football without rules, and features exaggerated tackles, late hits, and high-scoring affairs. To make the action more up-tempo than ordinary football titles, Xtreme uses a five-on-five setup, which puts an emphasis on skilled position players (quarterbacks, running backs, linebackers and cornerbacks)."
